# apps/mobile environment — copy to .env and fill. NEVER commit .env (gitignored).
# SUPABASE_URL / SUPABASE_ANON_KEY / WEB_URL are REQUIRED with no defaults —
# src/lib/env.ts throws at import time if any is missing. Nx auto-loads this
# app's .env (NX_LOAD_DOT_ENV_FILES), so run tests through nx; the Expo dev
# loop is `pnpm exec expo start` from apps/mobile.

# Tourism API ORIGIN — no /api/v1 suffix (the @tourism/core client adds it).
# While running through a real Metro dev session, src/lib/env.ts IGNORES this
# and derives the origin from Constants.expoConfig.hostUri instead — the LAN
# IP Metro is currently bound to (same one ./start-dev.ps1 auto-detects for
# the QR code) — with the API's own port (3000) swapped in. Survives network
# changes (home/school/hotspot) with ZERO manual edits; just restart Metro
# after switching Wi-Fi. On a physical device "localhost" would resolve to the
# PHONE, not your PC — that's what the derivation avoids.
# This value is the FALLBACK for everything that has no Metro session to
# derive from — jest, CI, and production/EAS builds — so it still needs to be
# a real reachable origin, not left blank. The live API is the sane default:
# ⚠️ 2026-08-20: that host currently serves the API under `/api`, while the
# generated client calls `/api/v1/*` — every request 404s until Render's
# `API_PREFIX` is set back to `api/v1` (see docs/05-runbooks/env-and-secrets.md).
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://api.nexora-travel.agency

# Supabase (same project as web/admin/API). Project Settings -> API.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://<ref>.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# The deployed web app origin — Account-tab legal links + password reset open it.
EXPO_PUBLIC_WEB_URL=https://www.nexora-travel.agency
